<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The closed fold: what stands in for a group's fields while its switch is off.

    Four of the ten sections are destinations that hide credential boxes behind an enable
    switch, so with everything off the page used to run heading / switch / rule / heading /
    switch / rule with a hole where the fields would be — which reads as a section that failed
    to load rather than one you haven't turned on. A dashed rule fills that space with the one
    thing it can honestly say: there is more here, folded away.

    Dashed rather than solid on purpose. The page grammar this app already writes in is
    "solid = structure, dashed = strips" (LedgerContextMenu's header comment); the intake page
    draws exactly this for an empty gram slot. So a dashed line is already the app's word for a
    space something belongs in.

    Shape "line" draws through the vertical centre of the view, so give it height to sit in.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="line">
    <stroke
            android:width="2dp"
            android:color="@color/fgColor"
            android:dashWidth="7dp"
            android:dashGap="7dp"/>
</shape>
